<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dhanya Manikya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1515">1515</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dhanya Manikya was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripura">Tripura</a> from about 1490 to 1515 and one of the most powerful rulers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manikya-dynasty">Manikya dynasty</a>. He expanded the kingdom into eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> and towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chittagong">Chittagong</a>, fighting the Bengal Sultanate under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alauddin-husain-shah">Alauddin Husain Shah</a>. He was a patron of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> temples, including the Tripura Sundari temple at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udaipur">Udaipur</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dhanya-manikya.jpg" alt="Dhanya Manikya" width="300" height="153" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Erstwhile Kingdom of Tripura · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dhanya_Manikya_Tanka.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
